BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261203T003000Z
DTEND:20261203T023000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall &amp\; LIVE@jacobs
SUMMARY:Baroque Orchestra – Ingrid Matthews\, director
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Repertoire to be announcedAbout the DirectorIngrid Matthews te
 aches baroque violin in the Historical Performance Institute at the India
 na University Jacobs School of Music. She served previously as music dire
 ctor of the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, gue
 st director\, and concertmaster for leading early music ensembles includi
 ng the New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Ear
 ly Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\,
  Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, a
 nd many others. She is also a member of San Francisco-based chamber ensem
 ble Musica Pacifica and has held teaching residencies at the University o
 f Southern California\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish
  College of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and others. First prize
 winner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music\
 , Matthews herself has served as a juror for competitions such as the Mau
 rice and Lillian Barbash International Bach Competition and the Indianapo
 lis Early Music Competition. She has received high critical acclaim for h
 er extensive discography\; her recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for 
 Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommendation for this
  music…on either period or modern instruments" by American Record Guide
 \, and her recording of Biagio Marini is included in the Norton Anthology
  of Music used by conservatories and universities worldwide. Meeting URL:
  https://liveatjacobs.music.indiana.edu/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Enjoy this performance from almos
 t anywhere in the world via</strong><a href="https://liveatjacobs.music.i
 ndiana.edu/"><strong>LIVE@jacobs</strong></a><strong>!<br /></strong></p>
 <p><em>Repertoire to be announced</em><br /><br /><strong>About the Direc
 tor</strong><br /><br /><strong>Ingrid Matthews</strong> teaches baroque 
 violin in the Historical Performance Institute at the Indiana University 
 Jacobs School of Music. She served previously as music director of the Se
 attle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, guest director\, 
 and concertmaster for leading early music ensembles including the New Yor
 k Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festi
 val Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica Angeli
 ca\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, and many others
 . She is also a member of San Francisco-based chamber ensemble Musica Pac
 ifica and has held teaching residencies at the University of Southern Cal
 ifornia\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish College of th
 e Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and others. First prizewinner in the 
 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music\, Matthews her
 self has served as a juror for competitions such as the Maurice and Lilli
 an Barbash International Bach Competition and the Indianapolis Early Musi
 c Competition. She has received high critical acclaim for her extensive d
 iscography\; her recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccompanied 
 Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommendation for this music…on ei
 ther period or modern instruments" by <em>American Record Guide</em>\, an
 d her recording of Biagio Marini is included in the <em>Norton Anthology 
 of Music</em> used by conservatories and universities worldwide.</p> Meet
 ing URL: https://liveatjacobs.music.indiana.edu/
