BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261203T233000Z
DTEND:20261204T010000Z
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 East 9th Street\, Bloomington\, IN
SUMMARY:Interactive Frequencies II: A Multimedia Concert
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a sensorial evening featuring time-based works de
 veloped through a collaboration between Eskenazi School's Interactive Art
  course and the Jacobs School's Music Performance &amp\; Media course. Wo
 rking with Jiji Kim\, Associate Professor of Guitar\, and Megan Young\, S
 enior Lecturer of Digital Art\, students develop contemporary composition
 s in a range of musical and visual styles. The evening also features a sp
 ecial screening of&#160\;ResursiveBodies\,&#160\;an interdisciplinary pro
 ject support by the KIX Lab and created by Dance\, Theater\, and Art facu
 lty. Together\, these works explore connections between sound\, image\, a
 nd human experience\, informed by guest lecturers on heart rate tracking 
 and public health outcomes.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for a sensorial evening featuri
 ng time-based works developed through a collaboration between Eskenazi Sc
 hool's Interactive Art course and the Jacobs School's Music Performance &
 amp\; Media course. Working with Jiji Kim\, Associate Professor of Guitar
 \, and Megan Young\, Senior Lecturer of Digital Art\, students develop co
 ntemporary compositions in a range of musical and visual styles. The even
 ing also features a special screening of&#160\;<em>Resursive</em><em>Bodi
 es\,&#160\;</em>an interdisciplinary project support by the KIX Lab and c
 reated by Dance\, Theater\, and Art faculty. Together\, these works explo
 re connections between sound\, image\, and human experience\, informed by
  guest lecturers on heart rate tracking and public health outcomes.</p>
